cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
title: embedded_types
abstract: >-
  Fixed widths, a machine word, and the compile-time machinery a C11 embedded
  library is written in. The exact widths are named once, the machine word is
  derived from the target's pointer width and refuses to guess where it cannot,
  and the machinery every library above would otherwise define for itself lives
  here: a static assertion, feature probes that ask the compiler rather than
  reading its identity, the attribute wrappers, the unaligned-access word, and
  the assertions that pin a dispatch table's members to consecutive slots. Header
  only, nothing allocated, nothing run at startup.
